MODULE bayes_opt
FORMAT Pseudocode.
PURPOSE resumable hyperparameter search, validation-only selection, progress figures,
                and full-training dispatch for one or more configurations
PAPER Section 5.1.4 and Table 2, PDF p. 22
DEPENDENCIES train_save_history.pseudo; specs/paper_settings.yaml

SEARCH CONTRACT
    Entry point is bayes_study with task mode tune and separate study_mode in search,train,search_train.
    There is no work at import time; study_mode is an explicit invocation argument.
    Study direction is minimize validation MAE on the original flow scale.
    Persist trials and state in a named SQLite study.
    Sampler family is TPE; pruner family is MedianPruner.
    Reported study has 80 trials, with at most 40 epochs per trial.
    PARAMETERS Sampler settings, pruner warmup/report cadence and random seeds.
    Store the sampler, pruner and seed settings in the run configuration.
    Trial 78 identifies the paper's reported best trial.
    Use validation metrics for tuning, stopping and checkpoint selection.

SEARCH SPACE
    alpha_decay: categorical {0.01,0.05,0.1,0.2,0.5}.
    base_lr: log-uniform real in [0.00001,0.01].
    dropout_prop: uniform real in [0,0.5].
    rnn_units: categorical {64,96,128,192}.
    channel: categorical {256,512,768}.
    PINN_value: log-uniform real in [0.00001,0.1].
    additional_distribution_dim: integer categorical {2,3,4,5}.
    additional_section_feature_dim: integer categorical {5,6,7,8}.
    Legacy 'PINN_value' maps to the generation-consistency initial weight w0.
    Legacy 'channel' maps to GAT feature dimension, not number of attention heads.
    Each parameter must map to an actual model/loss setting consumed during training.

PROCEDURE plot_bayes_search(csv_path,save_path=None,dpi=600)
    INPUT csv_path, save_path=None, dpi=600.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT progress figure receipt and best completed-trial record.
    Read a tabular export including number, value, state and trial parameters.
    REQUIRE unique integer trial numbers and a known minimization objective.
    Sort rows by trial number and retain failed/pruned trial status.
    completed <- rows with state COMPLETE and finite objective value.
    IF completed is empty:
        Emit an explicit 'no completed finite trial' summary.
        RETURN no_plot with trial metadata.
    END IF
    incumbent <- positive infinity.
    FOR each completed trial in order:
        incumbent <- minimum of previous incumbent and trial validation MAE.
        Store incumbent as best_so_far at that completed trial number.
    END FOR
    best_row <- completed row with minimum value and declared deterministic tie rule.
    Create an 8 by 4 inch figure, or a caller-declared publication size.
    Configure a serif font with an available fallback and embeddable PDF font settings.
    Plot completed trial validation MAE against actual trial number.
    Plot nonincreasing best_so_far curve using the same trial-number positions.
    Scatter and label the selected best completed trial.
    Show failed/pruned trials as gaps in the value curve.
    Label x-axis 'Trial' and y-axis 'Validation MAE (passengers per OD interval)'.
    Title 'Bayesian Optimization Progress'; add legible legend.
    Add annotation using point coordinates, with text inside the figure bounds.
    Include study ID and run provenance in figure metadata or a sidecar.
    IF save_path is supplied:
        Resolve output path inside the study output directory.
        Ensure the file extension matches the figure format; the export default is PDF.
        Save with embedded fonts and supplied dpi for any rasterized artists.
        Close figure handles after saving in unattended runs.
        Record source CSV hash and selected trial number.
    ELSE:
        RETURN figure object to the caller; display only when explicitly interactive.
    RETURN figure artifact metadata and best completed trial record.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE objective(trial)
    INPUT trial.
    PARAMETERS explicitly bound SearchContext and Table 2 parameter distributions.
    OUTPUT best validation MAE for a completed trial.
    Context is an explicitly bound SearchContext containing base_cfg and base_cfg_path, study directory,
        sampler/reporting policy, artifact registry and training entry point.
    REQUIRE STUDY_ENTRY has bound that context to this objective callback for this study.
    cfg <- deep copy of context.base_cfg, already validated as a search template.
    REQUIRE required dataset/artifact manifests are complete before sampling.
    trial_directory <- allocate an exclusive run directory using context.study_id and trial.number.
    cfg.mode <- train; cfg.train.run_kind <- search_trial.
    cfg.train.log_dir <- trial_directory / 'training', a not-yet-created child directory.
    Keep configuration files in the trial directory so _get_log_dir can create the empty training directory once.
    cfg.train.trial_number <- trial.number.
    cfg.train.base_lr <- trial.sample_log_uniform('base_lr',0.00001,0.01).
    cfg.train.optimizer_parameters.learning_rate <- cfg.train.base_lr in the same sampled-parameter update.
    cfg.model.dropout_prop <- trial.sample_uniform('dropout_prop',0,0.5).
    cfg.model.rnn_units <- trial.sample_categorical('rnn_units',[64,96,128,192]).
    cfg.model.channel <- trial.sample_categorical('channel',[256,512,768]).
    cfg.model.PINN_value <- trial.sample_log_uniform('PINN_value',0.00001,0.1).
    cfg.model.alpha_decay <- trial.sample_categorical('alpha_decay',
        [0.01,0.05,0.1,0.2,0.5]).
    cfg.model.additional_distribution_dim <- trial.sample_categorical(
        'additional_distribution_dim',[2,3,4,5]).
    cfg.model.additional_section_feature_dim <- trial.sample_categorical(
        'additional_section_feature_dim',[5,6,7,8]).
    cfg.train.epochs <- 40 as the maximum; pruning can end a trial earlier.
    cfg.evaluation.test_access <- disabled_during_search.
    Resolve model-dimensional dependencies and validate all sampled values are consumed.
    Prepare auxiliary encoder architectures compatible with sampled embedding dimensions.
    Reuse cached pretraining only when its full architecture/training-data key matches.
    Bind verified, dimension-compatible auxiliary artifacts and IDs into cfg.artifacts for this trial.
    Validate the fully resolved cfg for entrypoint=main_training,mode=train after those bindings.
    Keep RDS, split definition and evaluation policy identical across comparable trials.
    Record sampler seed and training seed according to the declared trial seed policy.
    resolved_config_path <- trial_directory / 'resolved_config.yaml'.
    Write the exact resolved configuration persistently at resolved_config_path.
    Write a temporary invocation config only if required by an executable adapter.
    invocation <- {entrypoint:main_training,config_filename:resolved_config_path,
        mode:train,resume_checkpoint:ABSENT}.
    Start each fresh trial from its own initialized state.
    callback <- MAKE_VALIDATION_CALLBACK(trial,context.reporting_policy,
        first_epoch=cfg.train.start_epoch,max_epochs=cfg.train.epochs).
    TRY:
        training_result <- train_save_history.main(args=invocation,
            validation_callback=callback,
            allow_test_evaluation=false).
        REQUIRE finite training_result.best_validation_mae.
        REQUIRE selected checkpoint was determined by validation only.
        Record checkpoint hash, best epoch and all immutable artifact IDs on trial.
        objective_value <- training_result.best_validation_mae.
    ON pruning:
        Preserve PRUNED state and the trial artifacts.
        Preserve the pruned trial's state and recorded intermediate values.
        Re-raise TrialPruned to record the PRUNED state.
    ON training failure:
        Record tensor/NaN failures and set the trial state to FAILED.
        Re-raise the original failure; only the study's explicit catch policy may continue other trials.
    FINALLY:
        Release model/device resources owned by this trial.
        Remove only that trial's known temporary invocation file after path validation.
        Preserve its resolved configuration, history and checkpoint manifests.
    RETURN objective_value only on successful completion.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE MAKE_VALIDATION_CALLBACK(trial,policy,first_epoch,max_epochs)
    INPUT active trial and its reporting policy.
    PARAMETERS first displayed epoch, maximum epoch count, report cadence and intermediate statistic.
    OUTPUT callback(epoch,validation_mae,checkpoint_manifest).
    completed <- 0; best_seen <- INFINITY.
    DEFINE callback(epoch,validation_mae,checkpoint_manifest):
        REQUIRE epoch=first_epoch+completed AND completed<max_epochs.
        report_step <- completed; completed <- completed+1.
        best_seen <- MIN(best_seen,validation_mae).
        IF policy.intermediate_statistic=current_epoch:
            intermediate_value <- validation_mae.
        ELSE:
            intermediate_value <- best_seen.
        END IF
        IF report_step matches policy.report_cadence:
            trial.report(value=intermediate_value,step=report_step).
            Append {report_step,epoch,checkpoint_manifest.epsilon,intermediate_value,checkpoint_manifest.id}
                to this trial's progress log.
            IF trial.should_prune():
                Save the partial-history and best-checkpoint references.
                RAISE TrialPruned.
            END IF
        END IF
    END CALLBACK
    RETURN callback.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE STUDY_ENTRY(args)
    INPUT normalized study invocation args.
    PARAMETERS study identity, SQLite path, search budget and final-configuration paths.
    OUTPUT study metadata and requested full-training results.
    REQUIRE args.entrypoint=bayes_study and args.mode=tune after the configuration adapter.
    mode <- args.study_mode; require mode in {search,train,search_train}.
    base_cfg_path <- args.config_filename.
    REQUIRE the study's base configuration path.
    base_cfg,config_provenance <- config.load_configuration(base_cfg_path,args.project_root,invocation=args).
    Use tune/study_mode validation here; train-only dispatch must not require a new search sampler/pruner.
    study_root <- validated base_cfg.base_dir / 'bayes_study'.
    Create study_root if needed, without clearing existing study files.
    storage_uri <- absolute SQLite database path under study_root.
    study_id <- explicit stable study name tied to model family and data manifest.
    Store dataset and objective signatures; obtain the search-space signature from the existing study in train-only mode.
    IF mode includes search:
        Compute and store the configured search-space signature before creating or resuming search.
        IF a study already exists:
            REQUIRE explicit resume semantics and matching signatures.
            Restore trial records from SQLite and sampler/pruner state from their declared state artifacts.
            A trial database alone is not proof that the sampler RNG trajectory was restored.
            IF such state is unavailable, label resumed suggestions a new stochastic continuation.
            Label continuation without a saved sampler state as a new stochastic continuation.
        ELSE:
            Create minimizing study with configured TPE and MedianPruner.
        END IF
        budget_semantics <- declared meaning of '80 trials' on resume.
        For a fresh study matching the paper's trial count, allocate 80 attempted trial slots.
        For resume, distinguish 80 total attempts from 80 additional attempts.
        Count COMPLETE, PRUNED, FAILED and RUNNING states according to stored policy.
        remaining <- declared total budget minus already-counted trials.
        REQUIRE remaining >= 0 or explicitly report the study already exceeds budget.
        Bind an immutable SearchContext to objective using the chosen adapter's closure mechanism.
        Include base_cfg,base_cfg_path,study_id,study_root,reporting policy and artifact registry explicitly.
        Optimize that bound objective for remaining slots, subject to declared resource/failure limits.
        Use database locking appropriate for any concurrent workers.
        Export number, state, value, sampled parameters, timings and error summaries.
        Persist sampler/pruner state at declared consistent boundaries if exact resume is supported.
        Save trials.csv atomically and record a snapshot ID.
        plot_bayes_search(trials.csv,study_root/'bayes_progress.pdf').
        Report best completed trial only when at least one valid trial exists.
    END IF
    IF mode includes train:
        REQUIRE an existing compatible study containing a finite completed trial.
        Load the selected best trial by the declared validation/tie rules.
        configs <- args.FINAL_CONFIG_FILES if nonempty, otherwise [base_cfg_path].
        REQUIRE all requested config paths exist and have unique resolved identities.
        FOR each cfg_path in configs:
            FULL_TRAIN_SELECTED_CONFIGURATION(cfg_path,best_trial,study_root).
        END FOR
    END IF
    RETURN study metadata and any full-training results.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE FULL_TRAIN_SELECTED_CONFIGURATION(cfg_path,best_trial,study_root)
    INPUT cfg_path, best_trial, study_root.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT full-training result and selected-checkpoint manifest.
    cfg_train <- a fresh parse of this cfg_path.
    original_epochs <- cfg_train.train.epochs.
    REQUIRE original_epochs is explicitly supplied for this configuration.
    Check model variant and feature switches are compatible with the searched study.
    IF applying selected parameters to an ablation, label it a declared transfer policy.
    Initialize replaced_params as an empty mapping.
    PARAMETER MAP:
        base_lr -> train.base_lr.
        dropout_prop -> model.dropout_prop.
        rnn_units -> model.rnn_units.
        channel -> model.channel.
        PINN_value -> model.PINN_value.
        alpha_decay -> model.alpha_decay.
        additional_distribution_dim -> model.additional_distribution_dim.
        additional_section_feature_dim -> model.additional_section_feature_dim.
    FOR each sampled key/value in best_trial.params:
        REQUIRE key exists in parameter map.
        destination <- parameter map[key].
        replaced_params[key] <- {old_value: cfg_train[destination],new_value:value}.
        cfg_train[destination] <- value.
    END FOR
    Validate all eight expected search keys exist in the selected trial.
    cfg_train.train.optimizer_parameters.learning_rate <- cfg_train.train.base_lr atomically with selection.
    Record the replaced optimizer rate too; no stale template rate may override the selected value.
    Restore cfg_train.train.epochs <- original_epochs.
    cfg_train.mode <- train and cfg_train.train.run_kind <- full_training.
    Clear any inherited train.trial_number search-control field.
    Store replaced_params, study ID, selected_trial_number and selection score under selection_provenance.
    Set test access policy to after_selection.
    final_training_directory <- allocate a unique directory using config stem and run ID.
    cfg_train.train.log_dir <- final_training_directory / 'training', initially absent.
    Copy the source config under an unambiguous 'source_config' name.
    Prepare matching auxiliary encoder artifacts for selected embedding dimensions.
    Store their verified immutable references in cfg_train.artifacts.
    resolved_config_path <- final_training_directory / 'resolved_config.yaml'.
    Write the exact resolved config to that path after every selected parameter and artifact ID is resolved.
    invocation <- {entrypoint:main_training,config_filename:resolved_config_path,
        mode:train,resume_checkpoint:ABSENT}.
    result <- train_save_history.main(args=invocation,validation_callback=ABSENT,
        allow_test_evaluation=true).
    REQUIRE training used validation-only checkpoint selection and sealed that choice before test access.
    Save the full training result, artifact manifest and selected checkpoint hash.
    RETURN result including best validation MAE and separately labeled test evaluation.
END PROCEDURE

PAPER REFERENCE VALUES
    Reported trial label: 78.
    Reported base_lr: 0.00653; dropout_prop: 0.442.
    Reported rnn_units: 96; channel: 256.
    Reported PINN_value: 0.0264; alpha_decay: 0.1.
    Reported distribution dimension: 5; section feature dimension: 6.
    Continuous reference values use the precision reported in the article.
    The reported_settings mode supplies these values directly without creating trial records.
